gitrl-f (0.6.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * A search shows each matching row of the list in bold, not only its hash.
  * The refs panel opens wide enough to show each name in full, to a limit of
    50 characters. After you drag its edge, it keeps the width that you chose.
  * The search field of the list stays in place when the count changes.
  * Match case, Regex and Display matches only are push buttons, not check
    boxes.
  * In the find bar of the diff, the Enter that searches also goes to the
    first match and opens its file.

 -- alexandros filotheou <alexandros.filotheou@gmail.com>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 20:13:06 +0200

gitrl-f (0.5.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * The name of the program changes from gittree to gitrl-f. The package is
    gitrl-f and the command is gitrlf. When you install the package gitrl-f,
    it removes the package gittree.
  * The command git tree is removed. Use gitrlf.
  * The PPA is ppa:li9i/gitrl-f. If you added ppa:li9i/gittree, remove it.
  * The settings, the ticks and the list of repositories of gittree do not
    move to gitrl-f. Set them again.
  * With no ref and no tick option, the ticks that you last chose in a
    repository come back.
  * One search bar above the list, opened with Ctrl+F, searches the
    messages, the changed lines or the files. Each search waits for Enter.
    Display matches only hides the other commits. The command line takes -S,
    -G and -i, as git log does.
  * While the pane is open, Ctrl+F finds a text in the diff, with Match case
    and Regex.
  * A right click on a file in the diff shows the history of the file,
    through its renames. A right click on a line shows the history of the
    line or of the selected lines, or goes to the commit that last changed
    the line.
  * The menu of a commit gives the branches and tags that have it, the first
    tag with it, and the merge that brought it into the branch of HEAD. The
    menu of a ref goes to where it splits from another ticked ref.
  * When a messages search finds a commit only on a ref that is not ticked,
    Tick and show ticks that ref and selects the commit.

 -- alexandros filotheou <alexandros.filotheou@gmail.com>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 16:38:58 +0200

gittree (0.4.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * The name of the program changes from gitree to gittree. The command is
    gittree, and git tree runs it too. When you install the package
    gittree, it removes the package gitree.
  * The PPA is ppa:li9i/gittree. If you added ppa:li9i/gitree, remove it.
  * The settings of gitree do not move to gittree. Set your preferences
    again.

